nt it's  materially relevant who is the  Democratic nominee to the future profits  of healthcare companies it would be very  naive to pretend that that's not what's  going on but then there's the next angle  Joe Biden has not made it a secret that  if he's president the main crossroads of  our are going to remain fundamentally  unchanged he actually was caught saying  this to donors and remember when Joe  Biden said I need you very badly to  wealthy donors no one standard of living  will change nothing would fundamentally  change rich people are just as patriotic  as poor people we may not want to  demonize anyone who has made money and I  hope if I win this nomination I won't  let you down that also applies to the  centers of industries so of course  markets like the Biden wins it's a  continuing gravy train for healthcare  stocks it's very good for them it's not  so good for people who need care and  can't afford it but that's why health  care stocks were up ten to fifteen  percent yesterday and then on top of  that there's always a layer with the  markets of predictability and  maintaining the status quo markets like  that Joe Biden said it he then won a  bunch of primaries you really don't have  to dig too deeply to figure out what's  going on here combined more generally  with this erratic nature of the market  under Trump up down up down  particularly with the cool party virus  as we are calling it you'll understand  why if you watched yesterday's show the  market is up and down drastically  already the highs are high the lows are  low  yesterday was a high and it was a  particularly good day for healthcare  stocks that are experiencing what we  could call some relief as a result of  the Super Tuesday results the question  is is what's good for healthcare stocks  good for the average American I think we  all know the answer to that
 

